{"name":"Impressionist","hex":"#8aa4ac","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"impressionist","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who adheres to the theory or method of impressionism.","A performer who does impressions; a mimic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impressionist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Impressionist (entertainment)","blocks":[{"text":"An impressionist or a mimic is a performer whose act consists of imitating sounds, voices and mannerisms of celebrities and cartoon characters. The word usually refers to a professional comedian/entertainer who specializes in such performances and has developed a wide repertoire of impressions, including adding to them, often to keep pace with current events. Impressionist performances are a classic casino entertainment genre."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/ObamaCrosson019.png/330px-ObamaCrosson019.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Impressionist_(entertainment)","wikidata":"Q1148872"},{"title":"Impressionism","blocks":[{"text":"Impressionism was a 19th-century art movement characterised by visible brush strokes, open composition, emphasis on accurate depiction of light in its changing qualities, ordinary subject matter, unusual visual angles, and inclusion of movement as a crucial element of human perception and experience. Impressionism originated with a group of Paris-based artists whose independent exhibitions brought them to prominence during the 1870s and 1880s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Claude_Monet%2C_Impression%2C_soleil_levant.jpg/330px-Claude_Monet%2C_Impression%2C_soleil_levant.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Impressionism","wikidata":"Q40415"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/The_Fightin